egin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,3=2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-9=1\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 6+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,10=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.$" 13194139535477 17592186045443 true] [17592186265744 1071 "Find $XY$,  if  $X=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $Y=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535477 17592186045443 false] [17592186265744 1071 "Find $XY$,  if  $X=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$" 13194139535477 17592186045443 true] [17592186265744 1074 "Here, $X$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $Y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $X$ and $3$ rows in $Y,$ so $X$ and $Y$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{X}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Y}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={XY}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $XY,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}22 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,22=5\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,9=5\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$XY=[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535477 17592186045443 false] [17592186265744 107